-- title:
--   Divisor presentation of an invertible ideal sheaf on a curve
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be a field and let $x \colon X \to \operatorname{Spec} K$ be a morphism with $X$ an integral scheme, $x$ separated, quasi-compact and smooth of relative dimension one; the function field $X.\mathrm{functionField}$ is a $K$-algebra through [`AlgebraicCurve.baseToFunctionField`](def/AlgebraicCurve_CurveModel.html#L18), the germ at the generic point of the map induced by $x$ on global sections. Let $I$ be a quasi-coherent ideal sheaf datum on $X$ satisfying `IsInvertible`: every point of $X$ lies in a basic open $X.\mathrm{basicOpen}\,f$ of an affine open $U$ such that, on the affine basic open attached to $f$, the ideal of $I$ is generated by a single non-zero-divisor. Then there are a divisor $D$ of $K(X)/K$ (a finitely supported integer-valued function on the places of $K(X)$ over $K$, a place being a proper valuation subring containing the image of $K$ whose ring is a principal ideal ring) and additive maps $\varphi_U \colon \Gamma(I.\mathrm{module}, U) \to K(X)$, for $U$ open in $X$, where $I.\mathrm{module}$ is the ideal sheaf viewed as an $\mathcal O_X$-module (the kernel of the unit-to-pushforward-unit map of the closed immersion it defines), such that: $\varphi$ commutes with restriction to nonempty opens; $\varphi_U(a \cdot m) = \mathrm{algebraMap}(a)\,\varphi_U(m)$ for nonempty $U$; $\varphi_U$ is injective for nonempty $U$; for nonempty affine $U$ the image of $\varphi_U$ is the $K$-subspace $\{ f : v(f) \le \exp(D v) \text{ for all places } v \text{ centred at a closed point of } U \}$; and for $s \in \Gamma(I.\mathrm{module}, U)$ generating the module on every open $W \le U$ containing a closed point $y \in U$, one has $\exp(D v) = v(\varphi_U(s))$ for every place $v$ whose valuation subring is the image of the stalk at $y$ in $K(X)$. Moreover there is $c \neq 0$ in $K(X)$ with $\varphi_U(m) = c \cdot \mathrm{algebraMap}$ of the image of $m$ under the inclusion $I.\mathrm{module} \to \mathcal O_X$, for all nonempty $U$ and all $m$, and such that whenever $U$ is affine, $y \in U$ is a closed point, the ideal of $I$ on $U$ is generated by $g \in \Gamma(X,U)$, and $v$ is a place with valuation subring the image of the stalk at $y$, then $D v + \operatorname{ord}_v(c) + \operatorname{ord}_v(g) = 0$, where $\operatorname{ord}_v(f) = -\log v(f)$.
--
--   This is the curve-theoretic identification of the ideal sheaf of an effective Cartier divisor $Z$ on a smooth curve: presented inside the function field it is $\mathcal O_X(-W(Z) - \operatorname{div} c)$, $W(Z)$ being the Weil divisor $\sum_y \operatorname{ord}_y(g_y)[y]$ attached to local equations $g_y$, the auxiliary function $c$ arising because the presentation is the one produced for a general invertible module by [`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.IsInvertible.exists_divisor_range_eq_lSpaceOn`](thm.html#AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.IsInvertible.exists_divisor_range_eq_lSpaceOn). It is used by [`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.isPrincipal_sub_single_of_presentation_ker_pow`](thm.html#AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.isPrincipal_sub_single_of_presentation_ker_pow) in the computation of divisor classes attached to ideal sheaves.
